From 205c3a07c1c4b73dde99270597401ccb1e8ae204 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:08:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] NAS: let the nrUE join a multicast MBS session

The UE could not ask to join one: there was no PDU Session Modification
Request encoder at all, and neither MBS container existed in either direction.

- MbsContainers.{c,h} encodes the Requested MBS container (TS 24.501 V18.14.0
  clause 9.11.4.30) and decodes the Received MBS container (clause 9.11.4.31),
  including walking over the optional fields -- addresses, service area,
  timers, security container -- that the UE has no use for yet but that have to
  be sized correctly or the next entry cannot be found.

- PduSessionModificationRequest.{c,h} encodes the message around it
  (clause 8.3.7), with the container as the type 6 IE 0x70 it is.

- The PDU Session Modification Command decoder takes IEI 0x71 and reports what
  the network decided, which the UE logs per session with the decision and,
  for a rejection, its cause (clause 6.3.2.3).

- --mbs-join <tmgi hex> names the session to join. The join is sent once a PDU
  session it can ride on is up, because clause 7.2.1.3 step 1 needs "an
  existing PDU session that can be used to send the UE join request", and only
  once. Giving the option to one UE's process and not another's is what lets a
  test decide which UE joins.

Acting on an accepted join -- a multicast MRB, a G-RNTI -- is the radio work
and is not here; what the UE does today is ask, and say what it was told.

nas_lib_test gains the octets of both containers checked against the clause,
the whole Modification Request, the optional-field skipping, the malformed
cases, and the parsing of --mbs-join's argument.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
